title: Cells in the Works
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and lw_cells_timer <= 0 and time >= 5
on-arrival: {!
Q.lw_cells_timer = 6;
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.lw_cells_played = (Q.lw_cells_played || 0) + 1;
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.card();
// a big district where the party is weak in the works: many workers, few of ours
RG.lw.setD(RG.lw.best(function (d) { return true; }, function (d) { return RG.lw.dv(d, 'militancy') - RG.lw.dv(d, 'loyalty') / 3 + Math.random() * 20; }));
!}
frequency: 150
is-card: true
tags: movement

= Cells in the Works

In **[+ lw_d_name +]**, the party is strong in the streets and weak at the bench. At [+ lw_works +], with thousands on the payroll, the party has a few dozen members, and they do not know each other. They meet as residents of [+ lw_town +], not as workers of the works, and the management has never had to think about them.

The district wants to build a factory cell: a group of comrades in each shop, with their own leaflet, meeting at the gates, answering to the party. How should it work?

- @cell: Build a party cell, with a works newspaper.
- @union: Win the union branch first.
- @stewards: Build a network of revolutionary shop stewards.
- @union_org: Build the revolutionary works organisation instead.
- @easy_discard

@cell
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Slow, solid work. The district gains members and listens to the Zentrale.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {members: 0.06, loyalty: 5});
Q.worker_support += 1;
RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 3);
!}

The cell meets in the canteen at the end of the night shift. Its first works paper, two duplicated sheets called "The Red Lathe", is read in every shop, and the foremen confiscate it, which is the best advertising it could have.

@union
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The branch meetings, the wage talks, the slow road. Support grows. The Right's line.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids working inside the reformist unions.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('union_work');
Q.worker_support += 3;
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {members: 0.03, loyalty: 2});
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 2, 4);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 0, -2);
!}

Our comrades go to every branch meeting of the metalworkers' union at [+ lw_works +], volunteer for every committee and never miss a vote. In six months, the branch secretary is one of ours.

@stewards
subtitle: Militant men in every shop, ready to stop the works at a signal. The Left likes it; so do the police.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {militancy: 5, guards: 0.3, repression: 3});
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 2, 4);
!}

A network of shop stewards takes shape, the way the revolutionary stewards of Berlin did it in the war: a man in every shop, a meeting place outside the works, and a signal for stopping work that the management does not know.

@union_org
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Out of the old unions, into a revolutionary union of the works. The Left Radicals' answer.
view-if: ultraleft_gone = 0
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('councils');
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {militancy: 6, loyalty: (Q.lw_d_fcode == 4 ? 6 : -3)});
Q.worker_support -= 1;
RG.lw.lean('ultraleft', 2, 5);
RG.lw.lean('unionist', -1, -4);
!}

The comrades tear up their union books in the canteen and found a works organisation of their own, with a red card and no officials. Five hundred join in the first week. The union expels the rest of our members at [+ lw_works +] in the second.
